WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.040
It's been some time since He-Man ruled the world,&nbsp;
but the once-mighty TV and toy phenomenon is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.200
finally ready for a reboot. Whether you're a&nbsp;
longtime fan or a newcomer, here are all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.000
reasons why Netflix's Masters of the Universe&nbsp;
will blow your mind from here to Eternia.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.120
It took what felt like forever, but&nbsp;
we now have a definitive answer:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.400
"Masters of the Universe: Revelation" will&nbsp;
debut on Netflix on Friday, July 23, 2021.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.400
When filmmaker Kevin Smith, the geek icon&nbsp;
producer of the "Revelation" miniseries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.280
first announced the show at&nbsp;
Anaheim's Power-Con 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.280
it was difficult to tell just how far along&nbsp;
the series was in the production pipeline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.560
But the team behind the show obviously&nbsp;
went right to work if they managed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.960
wrap up production in the year and half since&nbsp;
then while in the midst of a global pandemic.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.160
We should note that July 23 is&nbsp;
only the first part of the season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.240
with five episodes going up for streaming on&nbsp;
that date. Hopefully, we'll get some indication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.680
about the second batch of "Revelation"&nbsp;
episodes soon after the initial premiere.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.840
Smith took to Twitter in November 2019&nbsp;
to share that the voice cast was about to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.600
begin recording their parts, so that means&nbsp;
the second half shouldn't be too far away.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.560
If this is the case, Netflix will need&nbsp;
to figure out where it can fit the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.840
half of "Revelation" into its release&nbsp;
schedule; of course, we'll be keeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.080
an eye out for an official announcement, which&nbsp;
we expect to arrive sooner rather than later.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.960
Netflix doesn't shy away from positive PR when&nbsp;
they know viewers are flocking to a new show, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.600
shown when "Bridgerton" obliterated all previous&nbsp;
records for viewership on the streaming service.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.600
If "Masters of the Universe: Revelation" turns&nbsp;
out to be the hit that Netflix hopes it will be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.280
they won't waste any time moving up the release&nbsp;
of the remaining episodes for the series.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.440
"Masters of the Universe: Revelation" is&nbsp;
already proving to be far glitzier than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.840
the '80s series we all know and love with&nbsp;
its illustrious cast of triple-A talent.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.280
He-Man will have his shouts and war cries&nbsp;
powered by Chris Wood of "Supergirl"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.400
and "The Vampire Diaries" fame. The&nbsp;
biggest get of this series, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.920
is without a doubt Mark Hamill; in&nbsp;
a truly inspired casting choice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.440
he will be lending his incredible voice&nbsp;
talents to iconic villain Skeletor.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.520
Hamill may still be most well known for playing&nbsp;
Luke Skywalker in the "Star Wars" franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.920
but he's almost as famous for his stellar body of&nbsp;
voice acting work — he has consistently performed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.720
an animated version of the Joker since the '90s.&nbsp;
More recently, he has been putting his evil shriek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.360
to work as SkekTek the Scientist in the other&nbsp;
big '80s nostalgia revival series on Netflix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.440
"The Dark Crystal: Age of Resistance,"&nbsp;
so becoming Skeletor is a perfect fit for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.822
his style. What can we say? He's very&nbsp;
good at those unhinged evil cackles.

00:02:15.822 --> 00:02:20.893
"Here is the answer we seek.... Life everlasting!"

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.160
The celebrity train doesn't stop there, as we&nbsp;
continue down the long list of Eternia's friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:33.440
and enemies. The cast includes Sarah Michelle&nbsp;
Gellar as Teela; Liam Cunningham as Man-At-Arms;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.680
Lena Headey as Evil-Lyn; Diedrich&nbsp;
Bader as King Randor &amp; Trap Jaw;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.400
Alicia Silverstone as Queen Marlena, and many&nbsp;
more. There's even a role for Kevin Conroy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.240
the Batman to Hamill's Joker in "Batman:&nbsp;
The Animated Series," as Mer-Man.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.600
"Hello? Hello operator? I believe&nbsp;
my party's been disconnected."

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.800
Netflix's sparse webpage for the&nbsp;
upcoming "Masters of the Universe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.360
Revelation" series has a brief one-sentence&nbsp;
blurb as a summary of the show. That reads:

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.440
"After a calamitous battle fractures&nbsp;
Eternia, Teela and an unlikely alliance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.280
must prevent the end of the Universe&nbsp;
in this sequel to the '80s classic."

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.520
Exciting, eh? Netflix's teaser doesn't&nbsp;
provide much more context than that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.920
but by the power of Grayskull, it does feel&nbsp;
like a direct continuation of the 80s series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:21.840
complete with 95 seconds of action set to&nbsp;
Bonnie Tyler's "Holding Out for a Hero."

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.280
"At the beginning of our first episode,&nbsp;
it plays for the first ten minutes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.400
like a slightly, or way-better&nbsp;
animated version of the old show."

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.280
There is an interesting nugget&nbsp;
buried in the producing credits:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.720
the VP of Mattel TV, Rob David. At first blush,&nbsp;
that's no big deal, because it's very common for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.400
executives of intellectual properties&nbsp;
to receive executive producing credit.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.800
The twist here is that Rob David also came up&nbsp;
with the story for a 15-issue "He-Man" comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:54.240
series titled "The Eternity War" that&nbsp;
was published by DC from 2014 to 2016.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.080
The comics' story isn't centered&nbsp;
only on Skeletor and He-Man. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.880
it's about a no-holds-barred war for the soul&nbsp;
of Eternia, with big battles, noble sacrifices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.840
and bloody carnage. While this new Netflix&nbsp;
miniseries is likely not a direct adaptation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.080
elements from the comics could be incorporated.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.760
What the plot of "Revelation" will probably&nbsp;
not include, considering their absence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.000
from the cast list, is He-Man's sister&nbsp;
She-Ra and her many ancillary characters.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.840
Netflix's "She-Ra and the Princesses of&nbsp;
Power" animated series has no announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.280
connection to Revelation, and the two&nbsp;
shows likely won't connect at all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.120
because "She-Ra" has been running just&nbsp;
fine on its own steam for four seasons.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.880
It appears that we'll just have to wait to see&nbsp;
exactly what kind of story Smith and company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:37.360
are cooking up for us. Fortunately, the wait is&nbsp;
nearly over, and with all of the love that Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:42.000
David, and the rest of the crew are pouring into&nbsp;
this adaptation, we're not worried in the least.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.440
If you had any worries about the professional&nbsp;
credentials of the crew behind the scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:49.200
the composer for "Masters of the Universe:&nbsp;
Revelation" should ease your fears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.600
The animated Netflix show's composer is none&nbsp;
other than the award-winning Bear McCreary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.120
Longtime fans of "The Walking Dead" were&nbsp;
introduced to his music from the first moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:02.000
of the opening credits, and he remains one of the&nbsp;
longest-tenured people attached to the AMC show.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.600
His career has spanned multiple genres&nbsp;
and mediums. McCreary got his start in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.680
television on the 2004 version of "Battlestar&nbsp;
Galactica," where he scored almost all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.600
76 episodes of the sci-fi hit that&nbsp;
spawned a new generation of fans.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.160
From there, he continued his&nbsp;
work on television by composing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.160
music for several seasons of "Eureka" and&nbsp;
"Terminator: The Sarah Connor Chronicles."

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.120
McCreary's film work is rooted in&nbsp;
horror, where he created the music&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.120
for films like "Rest Stop" and "Wrong&nbsp;
Turn 2: Dead End." As his star rose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.680
he scored bigger and more widely known movies,&nbsp;
including "10 Cloverfield Lane," "Godzilla:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.120
King of the Monsters," and the&nbsp;
2019 reboot of "Child's Play."

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.760
One of his biggest professional&nbsp;
accomplishments in recent years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:40.720
however, has come in the form&nbsp;
of video games: specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:45.600
2018's "God of War." The PlayStation&nbsp;
4 exclusive was a mega hit for Sony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:50.160
selling more than 10 million copies in a little&nbsp;
over a year after its release. For his work on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.440
Norse mythology-inspired action epic, McCreary won&nbsp;
a BAFTA and four Game Audio Network Guild awards.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:59.120
Kevin Smith revealed McCreary as&nbsp;
the composer in February 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:03.040
and the @NetflixGeeked Twitter account posted a&nbsp;
video of Smith's reaction to hearing the "metal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:07.680
maestro's" work for the first time. Smith is&nbsp;
left visibly teary-eyed by the end of the clip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.680
which should tell fans of "Revelation" that&nbsp;
the music is in the most capable of hands.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.240
For those of you who just can't wait until&nbsp;
July 23, Dark Horse Comics is getting a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.000
top-tier team of writers and artists to hold&nbsp;
you over before "Masters of the Universe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.040
Revelation" premieres. Four issues of a prequel&nbsp;
comic, also titled "Masters of the Universe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:29.680
Revelation," are scheduled for release, with&nbsp;
#1 now available for pre-order everywhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:33.680
comics are sold. Kevin Smith and Rob David,&nbsp;
two of the names behind the Netflix show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:37.600
are also in charge of writing the comic&nbsp;
series, along with Tim Sheridan, known for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.760
his work on the "Superman: Man of Tomorrow"&nbsp;
and "Reign of the Supermen" animated movies.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:46.000
The comic has some heavyweights in the visual&nbsp;
department, as well, with drawings by Mindy Lee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.640
known for the comics "Bounty" and "Crimson Lotus",&nbsp;
color from Rico Renzi, who you may know from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:55.600
comics "Spider-Gwen" and "Sundowners", and letters&nbsp;
by Deron Bennett, known for his work on "Batgirl."

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:00.160
Stjepan Sejic, a veteran of "He-Man: The&nbsp;
Eternity War," drew the cover of the first issue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:03.280
and Dave Wilkins will provide covers&nbsp;
for the remaining three issues.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.760
Each issue will have at least one variant&nbsp;
cover, drawn by many other talented artists.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.080
The release of a comic book&nbsp;
for "Masters of the Universe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:14.800
Revelation" is a nice callback to the original&nbsp;
'80s cartoon, which also contained comic books&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.960
that were included with the release of each new&nbsp;
action figure. This prequel is said to explore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.200
the aftermath of an attack on King Randor,&nbsp;
He-Man's father. The creature sent in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.600
attack is somehow linked to He-Man's sword,&nbsp;
and he sets off after Skeletor and Evil-Lyn.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:32.640
"Masters of the Universe: Revelation" #1 will hit&nbsp;
comic shelves and digital storefronts on July 7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:38.320
2021. The other three issues will release on&nbsp;
August 11, September 8, and October 13, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:42.080
should help hold us over until the second half&nbsp;
of the "Revelation" series premieres on Netflix.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:46.640
As we mentioned earlier, "Masters of the&nbsp;
Universe: Revelation" isn't the only revival&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:51.200
of this series in the works for Netflix. Mattel&nbsp;
and Netflix are also collaborating on a totally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:55.040
separate production, simply titled "He-Man&nbsp;
and the Masters of the Universe." Unlike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:59.040
the anime-inspired "Revelation," this show&nbsp;
will reportedly be a more traditional take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:03.920
on the "Masters of the Universe" mythos, with the&nbsp;
target audience reportedly skewing much younger.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.280
At the moment, details on this&nbsp;
new "He-Man" show are very scarce.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:11.680
We know that the storylines will be new, and&nbsp;
that Skeletor is the center of the conflict.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.920
The onslaught of "He-Man" lore hasn't stopped&nbsp;
there. An additional "He-Man and the Masters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:19.920
of the Universe" animated film is also in&nbsp;
the works, as well as a live-action movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.440
No matter what, it'll probably be better&nbsp;
than the last time they tried that.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.000
"I'll be back!"

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.160
Check out one of our newest videos right here!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:31.760
Plus, even more Looper videos about&nbsp;
your favorite stuff are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:39.840
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

